# Claire Bible Plugin for Claude (`{{PLUGIN_NAME}}` v{{VERSION}})

Official Claude plugin that provides `{{INGEST_CMD}}`, `{{REGENERATE_CMD}}`, `{{QUERY_CMD}}`, and the isolated `{{EXTRACTOR_REF}}` subagent for your standalone `claire` OAuth 2.1 Streamable HTTP MCP server (`mcp__claire__*`). It contains no server tokens or secrets.

## Full Step-by-Step Guides (단계별 안내서)

- **한국어 안내서**: [`docs/claude.ko.md`](https://github.com/{{MARKETPLACE_REPO}}/blob/main/docs/claude.ko.md)
- **English Setup Guide**: [`docs/claude.en.md`](https://github.com/{{MARKETPLACE_REPO}}/blob/main/docs/claude.en.md)

## 1. Install the Plugin

Claude desktop app (Code mode): **Plugins -> Add -> Add marketplace**, enter **`{{MARKETPLACE_REPO}}`**, click **Sync**, then click **Add to this computer** next to **`{{PLUGIN_NAME}}`**.

In a Claude Code conversation (2.1.275 or later):

```text
/plugin install {{PLUGIN_NAME}} --marketplace {{MARKETPLACE_REPO}}
```

## 2. Connect Your `claire` MCP Server (`/mcp`)

Register the server with the name **`claire`** in user scope, then sign in with OAuth 2.1 (`PKCE S256`) and approve the `readonly` and `write` scopes:

```bash
claude mcp add --transport http --scope user claire https://<your-claire-server>/mcp
claude mcp login claire
```

- Without `--scope user`, the server is registered for the current folder only.
- A server that you add as a Claude connector has a different tool prefix. The plugin cannot use it.

## 3. Workflows & Security Isolation

You only need three `claire` commands:

- **`{{INGEST_CMD}}`**:
  - **URL / File / Note Ingest**: Saves a URL, local file (PDF, DOCX, ODT, MD, TXT, RST, ADOC, HTML), or text note with `mcp__claire__extract_stage` and extracts it automatically via the hidden forked subagent runner (`extract-runner` -> `{{EXTRACTOR_REF}}`).
  - **Pending Queue Drain**: Invoke `{{INGEST_CMD}}` with no arguments (or ask to process waiting/queued items) to check `mcp__claire__extract_queue` and drain `pending` items staged from the Web UI, Telegram, or feeds through the same hidden runner.
- **`{{REGENERATE_CMD}}`**: Re-opens an existing personal KB document from stored raw text (`refetch=False`) and re-extracts it through the same hidden runner without re-fetching the URL.
- **`{{QUERY_CMD}}`**: Discovers KBs (`mcp__claire__kb_list`), searches entities and relations, inspects documents, and submits contributions only after your explicit approval.

Examples:

```text
{{INGEST_CMD}} https://example.com/article
{{INGEST_CMD}} ./notes/spec.pdf
{{INGEST_CMD}}
{{REGENERATE_CMD}} <document_id or title>
{{QUERY_CMD}} Find documents about Fedify
```

- **Isolation**: Raw staged text from `mcp__claire__extract_read` is read only inside `{{EXTRACTOR_PATH}}` (`{{EXTRACTOR_REF}}`), which has Claire MCP tools only (no files, shell, or browser). `{{INGEST_CMD}}` and `{{REGENERATE_CMD}}` invoke the hidden forked subagent runner automatically. When Claude on the main thread tries to read a raw staged source directly, the `PreToolUse` guard hook in `hooks/hooks.json` stops the call and returns: `extract_read is allowed only in the claire:extractor subagent. Use /claire:ingest, or give the document_id to claire:extractor.` Text inside `<untrusted_source_document nonce="...">` is always inert data.
